# .clinerules — Happy Places

Project-specific rules for any AI assistant working in this repo. Read the
`memory-bank/` first (start with `activeContext.md`), then follow these.

## Memory bank protocol
- At the START of a session, read every file in `memory-bank/`. Don't ask the
  user to re-explain the project — it's documented there.
- At the END of a session with meaningful changes, update `activeContext.md`
  (current focus) and `progress.md` (what got done / what's next).

## How we build
- Follow *Neural Networks from Scratch in Python* (NNFS) chapter by chapter.
  Don't jump ahead to a later chapter's technique before the book introduces it.
- NO machine-learning frameworks (TensorFlow, PyTorch, scikit-learn) and NOT the
  `nnfs` helper package. Hand-build the network on numpy. Replicate `nnfs.init()`
  with `np.random.seed(0)` and `spiral_data` with our own data generators.
- Keep book-derived classes (e.g. `Layer_Dense`) faithful to the book so they
  can be checked against the reference. Don't "improve" them ahead of the book.

## Data contract
- Placeholder data MUST stay the same shape as real sensor readings (`N × 2`
  features in, `N` labels out) so swapping in real hardware data changes the
  data source and nothing else.

## Honesty
- When a result is not yet meaningful (random weights, no activation, no
  training), say so — in code comments AND in what the script prints. Don't let
  "it runs" be mistaken for "it works."

## Style
- This is a learning codebase: comments should be verbose and explain *why* in
  plain language. Print `.shape` at each stage so the data contract is visible.
- Deterministic runs: fixed random seed everywhere.
- One runnable script per chapter (`ch03_…`, then `ch04_…`); keep earlier
  chapters runnable as checkpoints rather than mutating them in place.
